WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:10.330
Welcome to Data Management. In this lesson, we explore this purpose: Define consistent ownership, organization and controls for business data.

2
00:00:10.330 --> 00:00:20.140
Consider this scenario. Two departments define the same metric differently. First understand the problem before producing documentation.

3
00:00:20.140 --> 00:00:30.750
Start with two steps: Identify data needs and owners. Then Define architecture and metadata. Each step should be explained and evidenced.

4
00:00:30.750 --> 00:00:40.620
Continue with Control data lifecycle activities. Then Review governance and usage. Verify the results against the intended outcome.

5
00:00:40.620 --> 00:01:00.580
Stronger evidence looks like this: Stronger: contemporaneous data catalog, ownership matrix, retention rules tied to real work. Weaker evidence would be: Weaker: keeping data without owners, metadata or governance; no trace of consistent use. Triangulate independent sources.

6
00:01:00.580 --> 00:01:14.830
Now your turn. Review four documents and two interviews, identify inconsistencies and complete the mastery challenge. This video is an independent teaching explanation, not official CMMI model wording.
